00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.140
Welcome Back to Kamogawa!

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.150
Are you ready, milady?

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:41.860
Yes.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.080
We will now initiate the third Vox Particle Control Experiment.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.870
Stage One.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.000
Connecting the Nerve Cutter to the Consciousness Strata.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.470
Stage Two. Activating Mind Probe.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:07.470
Penetrating straight into the Fourth Layer of the Consciousness Strata.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.110
Bio-telepathic wave pulse is in sync.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.650
Biometrics pattern, range beta to theta, is orange.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.110
What is the concentration of Vox particles?

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.030
It's stalling at around 200.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.410
Still far from the breaking point.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.540
Let us move on to Stage Three.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.540
Commencing Stage Three.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.290
Mind probe now penetrating the Sixth Layer, into the Ego Borderline Stratum.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.640
The cell structure in her Consciousness Bubble is becoming unstable.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.560
Any further stimulus may cause irremediable damage to her psyche.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.350
Pull the probe back to the Fifth Layer...

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.400
No, keep going.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.770
King Dizelmine?

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.700
This could inflict severe damage to Lady Lan's subconscious...

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.030
We don't have enough data yet.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.830
As you wish, your highness.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.910
Control, report.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:14.960
It's an enemy attack!

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.540
Armed forces from De Metrio are approaching!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.790
The enemy crafts have activated their weapons systems.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.000
They are attacking!

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.400
Lympha, standing by for takeoff.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.990
Lan, we are abandoning this station.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:51.990
Brother?!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.410
We are ready for takeoff.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.660
Jam enemy com systems and deploy!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.920
This facility is useless to us now that Villagiulio has discovered it.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.830
I understand.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.420
In that case, I will cover your escape.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.220
Dizelmine!

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.830
Thank you for your patience!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.460
Here's your Oraga Bowl lunch special!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.710
Please enjoy!

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.470
Madoka, I can handle the rest.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.930
Can you go help out the guys at the seaside cafe?

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.810
It's gonna get busy there soon.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.940
Sure thing, Uncle.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.690
On my way.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:10.700
<i>I better start thinking about what's really best for her future.</i>

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.620
Seaside Branch

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:15.660
Seaside Branch

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.750
Welcome.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.540
What a hottie...

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.500
Izo!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.880
BWH lunches: slightly better than the competition!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.090
Here are your Offshore lunch specials. Thank you for waiting!

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:35.100
Array, you're so cute!

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.480
Did you notice the customers over on the deck?

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.230
Yeah, they're from Le Garite.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.230
Just leave 'em alone.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.900
It's not so uncommon to see them around these days.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.440
You guys seem pretty busy.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.400
Kyouno!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.320
My uncle asked me to give you guys a hand.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.620
You're very welcome to, Kyouno!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.120
The guys come around when you're here.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.700
Array only attracts the strange ones.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:05.540
We've got a few who come all the way from Tokyo to see him.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.670
I don't choose the customers.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:08.960
Everyone is welcome.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.590
You know, you three are really starting to embrace your roles.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.890
Someone's drowning!

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.270
Oh no!

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.440
I'm coming!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.160
She's okay now.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.450
Success!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.040
Madoka!

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.760
Madoka, you're on the ball, as always.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.260
One never retires from the Jersey Club.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.890
More like the School Swimsuit Club.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.180
Either way, it's pretty unusual.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.560
Unusual?

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:04.350
Anyway, I still can't get over the fact that your uncle opened up a beach cafe.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.480
There was some talk about it a while ago.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:11.980
But until last year, it would've been impossible with just my uncle and myself to run the business.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.910
He should stick to easy dishes like curry and ramen noodles here.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.120
My uncle takes pride in his cooking.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.290
Did things change this year then?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.580
Yup. He found an awesome part-time chef.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.790
You mean Izocchi? But he's an alien.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.050
Not the sort of skill you'd expect from him.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.300
We decided to let those three run the place,

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.090
and it worked out great.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:40.800
Well, Kirikiri and Array aren't bad looking...

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.520
It's not Kirikiri. It's Kirius!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.350
Whatever.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.730
A lot of students from our school have become regulars.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.060
Take a look.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.280
Damn it, this isn't a host club.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.700
Is it any wonder this place is popular?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.990
All three are from outer space.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.120
Does that even matter?

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.200
Of course.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.580
I mean, it's sort of romantic.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.580
I dunno, they don't come across as the romantic type to me.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:12.630
Besides, more and more people from Le Garite have been coming over.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.840
That's the real reason for your last-minute college change, isn't it?

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.510
Oh really?

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.220
You've always wanted to study astronomy, right?

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.850
Now, I'm interested in diplomacy.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:25.930
Diplomacy?

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:31.940
Yes. From now on, we'll be dealing with people from Earth, Le Garite and more.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.980
So I thought that if I became a diplomat,

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.030
I'd be able to visit all kinds of planets.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.780
Wow... That sounds pretty awesome.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.450
It's still just a dream, though.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:45.450
Compared to that, my career plan is pretty down-to-earth.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.700
You're planning to find a job in Tokyo, right?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:48.750
No no...

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:51.710
I'm eyeing the Kamogawa Fisheries Cooperative now.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.710
Fisheries Cooperative?

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.540
You're going to use Koujirou's personal connections?

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.670
That too.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.760
But this place is perfect for surfing.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:04.850
Plus, Kamogawa's become the center of the world lately.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.640
It's gathering more interest than Tokyo at the moment.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.190
Madoka...

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.610
Will Lan and Muginami ever return to Kamogawa?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.740
I guess that wasn't the best choice of topic, huh.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.910
They're both busy.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.750
I bet they'll show up out of the blue, one day.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.460
You're right.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.920
It hasn't even been a year. I'm sure they'll come back.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.140
I wonder if Lan's learned how to swim?

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.180
t

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.180
t

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.130
Hey, Muginami!

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.880
Hey, Lan!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.900
I wonder if they're doing okay...

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:48.660
No, no! I have lots to do tomorrow.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:49.660
Time for bed!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.130
All sections, confirm anchor stabilization,

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.170
then turn in your checklists to the bridge.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.760
Jim, please report to HQ that we have reached Kamogawa.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:06.680
Roger.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.970
<i>We will hold an Intergalactic Conference on Pharos.</i>

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.100
<i>It will take place in Kamogawa!</i>

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.890
<i>I want you to head there immediately.</i>

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.230
So we're back here again...

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:24.650
Morning! Let's make this another great day, guys!

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.820
What's wrong?

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.070
Pharos?

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.450
They must've arrived late last night.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.750
So you didn't know about this, Kyouno?

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.000
No, I didn't.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.000
What about you? Did Asteria not tell you anything?

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:43.250
That girl has forgotten we even exist.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.960
I wonder if something happened.

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:46.840
Maybe they're on summer vacation.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:50.600
Madoka...

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:56.940
Lan?

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.190
Woof.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.150
Lan!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.530
Welcome back!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.120
You're looking good. Did you grow out your hair?

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.630
My aide evens it out for me every day.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.920
Spoken like a true princess!

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.300
You haven't changed at all, Madoka.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.590
Actually, she wasn't quite herself until you came back.

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:31.260
It's been a long time, Mr. Hiroshi.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.100
Is this for me?

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.730
Of course! Eat up.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.520
Thank you.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.690
Is it good?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.860
Yes, delicious.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.910
What's wrong?

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.280
Did you put wasabi in it, Uncle?

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.370
Huh? Why would I?

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.290
I'm sorry. It's nothing.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.160
How is everyone in Kamogawa?

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:00.830
Huh?

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.630
Oh yeah, they're all fine.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:04.880
And Youko?

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.420
She's in Madagascar.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.050
Madagascar?

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.350
It's faint, but I'm getting Vox particle readings.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.020
There's no mistaking it.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:28.320
It's a fossilized Lagrange Flower.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.490
I see... So she's there to investigate the Voxes.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:34.660
What about you? Is your older brother doing well?

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:35.450
Yes.

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.740
Yeah? That's great!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.250
We'll have to throw you a "welcome back" party!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.170
Madoka...

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:43.290
Huh?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:44.500
Will you hear me out?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.460
Lan?

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:48.760
I have a favor to ask.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.590
What is it?

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.930
Damn it! I can't hear them.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.850
What are they talking about?

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.440
Why would Le Garite's princess come here, and why now?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:04.060
Izo!

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.280
Vox Lympha?!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:13.990
Let's go!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.250
I'd like to order please.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.210
Water please!

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.120
Right away!

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:29.630
<i>Damn it! If only Kirius and Izo would hurry and get back here!</i>

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:34.470
I wish I could say it's good to have you and Kyouno back on board...

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.800
...but barging in unannounced in your \h Vox was a surprise to say the least.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:42.180
I'm here by special ordnance from King Dizelmine of Le Garite.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.810
This is an unofficial visit, but one of utmost importance.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:51.030
Then you came fully aware that Pharos was heading to Kamogawa.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:51.820
Lan...?

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.660
Madoka, please pilot Aura one more time.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.570
Huh?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:57.570
But...

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:01.370
Aura shut itself down after its last battle.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.580
You know this very well.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.500
Yes, I understand. But...

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.710
Our need is dire!

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.840
Lan...

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:18.800
In order to maintain our military power, we tried to reboot Aura.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.930
We conducted many tests with Madoka's help,

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.310
but they've all been unsuccessful.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:27.190
Well, even if they had worked, there was nothing for me to do.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.650
You're wrong!

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:29.310
Lan?

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.900
The connection you shared with Vox Aura runs deep.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.900
It's a bond that cannot be easily broken!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.360
You think so?

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.030
I know she'll move if you get in, Madoka.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.160
I already tried several times.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.630
But if you say so, I'll try it again.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.800
So what do I do... comrade?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.340
Comrade...

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:02.850
Tadokoro speaking.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.270
What?

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:07.690
We have a lot of guests today.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.520
The unidentified craft will soon enter our air defense identification zone.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.980
Does it belong to the Le Garite?

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:17.110
We made an inquiry, but the reply we received did not match any of Le Garite's.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.820
Order all ships to Defcon 2 status.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.120
The unidentified craft is quickly approaching.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:23.870
No!

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:25.120
Could this be...?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.710
What's going on? Snap out of it and report!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:29.120
P-Pardon me!

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.210
According to our IFF systems,

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:36.590
the unidentified craft is Vox Ignis. It's Muginami{desu}!

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.260
Muginami?!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.100
Lan, Muginami has returned too!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:45.430
She's running interference again...

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:51.850
Wait, Lan!

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:53.520
Hey, Lan!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.730
What's going on?!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.110
Lan...?

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.490
Don't worry. I will protect you, Madoka.{Man I've never heard that line before}

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:02.820
Huh?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.330
That girl...

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.870
Muginami is planning to kill you.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.420
Let's go, Orca.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.970
Muginami is... planning to what?

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.980
Orca...

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.890
So Lan is here, after all.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.060
Muginami!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.150
So you intend to have Madoka pilot the Vox no matter what?

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.240
Fine!

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.450
I'll destroy you first, Lan!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:54.380
Lord Villagiulio, Muginami has left the main force and has headed for Earth onboard Vox Ignis.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.500
What?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:59.630
I believe she intends to go after Kyouno Madoka by herself.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.380
Oh, brother...

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:06.260
I guess she's not cut out for De Metrio's regular army after all.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.010
What shall we do, sir?

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.600
She chose to carry out the dirty work in my name.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.140
What do you want me to do?

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:15.610
Have her court-martialed and executed?

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.820
But we can't just ignore her...

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.480
Let her be.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.900
Otherwise, we'd be no different from Dizelmine.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:26.910
Tell everyone that Muginami went to Earth under my orders.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.540
Yes, sir.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.920
My goodness...

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.500
They're way too gentle. Each and every one of them.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.000
Move! Please, Midori!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:44.130
Lympha, Ignis... Still engaged in battle.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.680
Lan... Muginami...

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:51.680
I don't get it. Why?

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.570
Why are you two fighting?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:11.080
This is crazy!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.790
Midori...

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:17.830
We've rested more than enough, don't you think?

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:21.050
It's time to get up.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:24.880
It's already a new semester!

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.340
Time to wake up,

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:27.340
sleepyhead!

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.970
Owww!

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.150
Midori!

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:41.730
Aura has activated!

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:42.650
What?!

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:50.160
Don't you dare start a fight without me!

